> Inspect the actual saved results

The figures below read actual saved outputs from this run. Native graph previews appear above the complete program. Reconstructed-task results retain the source budgets and are not reported as original benchmark scores.

> Actual published embedding geometry

Cosines use the eight saved pooled states. Request indices follow the source request list above. This pooling geometry is a serving diagnostic, not a claim of sentence-similarity training.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pretrained_bert_serve_cosine.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;auto arrays=n::load_npz("build/nn-completion/models/pretrained_bert_serve/outputs.npz");auto it=std::find_if(arrays.begin(),arrays.end(),[](const auto&a){return a.first=="bert_encoder";});if(it==arrays.end())throw std::runtime_error("actual published pooled states missing");auto h=it->second;auto unit=h/n::sqrt(n::sum(n::square(h),{1},true));auto cosine=n::matmul(unit,unit,false,true);auto values=cosine.to_vector<double>();std::vector<std::vector<double>>z(8,std::vector<double>(8));std::vector<double>x(8);std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),0.);for(int i=0;i<8;++i)for(int j=0;j<8;++j)z[i][j]=values[i*8+j];dm::graphics::RPlot::create().image(x,x,z).title("Actual published BERT pooled-state cosine").x_label("Request index in the source request list").y_label("Request index").size(900,750).save_svg("build/pretrained_bert_serve_cosine.svg");}
